These files contain measured functional constants, short format and bank identifiers,
and independent verification cases used by Slopesmith, Snowknife, and Unity.
The world layout contains relative scalar-field offsets and course-slot identifiers,
without executable addresses, instructions or a retail settings table.
The celestial spoke pattern is original OpenSlope presentation data, first authored
for Slopesmith. It does not reproduce the retail engine's arbitrary spoke table.
The board-audio contract contains original OpenSlope mix/response tuning,
verified through the public Slopesmith audio APIs and behavior documentation.
It contains no retail expression program.
The music-playback contract contains original OpenSlope mix and transition tuning,
verified through the public Slopesmith music API and behavior documentation.
The surface-spray contracts contain independently recovered functional scalar
values and relative field positions, checked against clean Trailmap 310/380 and
the shared motion response table. They contain no executable addresses or code.
The measured functional facts are documented in the local Trailmap research workspace. No retail executable,
disc image, extracted asset, or bulk disassembly is included or licensed here.
